      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thanks for reporting this issue. A future SDK release will no longer overwrite the scene at `Assets/Scenes/VRCDefaultWorldScene.unity` with the default VRChat world template scene when reopening a world project after deleting its Library folder.\n\nRegarding your suggestion to not automatically save the default scene - we agree this would be better practice, however there's an issue affecting Unity 2022.3.22f1 that can be reproduced in a standalone project:\n\n- Create a scene from a template that has at least one copied dependency in it.\n\n- Without saving the scene, enter play mode and then exit it again.\n\n- Save the scene. Dependencies used by the scene that should be cloned are not saved alongside it.\n\n- Close and reopen the project. The scene is now missing its copied dependencies. For the default VRChat world scene, this means all of its materials go missing.\n\nGiven this issue, the SDK will continue saving the scene by default for now to avoid having new creators run into this problem. The fix for this issue means it should now only recreate the scene if it doesn't already exist, though.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
